id: pm-vcs-merge-state-schema
title: Validate persisted merge-state structure before constructing continuation objects
description: "PR 150 branch-coverage audit found that readMergeState parses JSON as MergeState without structural validation. A persisted null ours reaches mergeContinue object construction and then the existing publication closure check refuses its invalid parent. HEAD, index and merge state remain unchanged. Retain the current refusal behavior in PR 150; separately validate malformed stored state before creating continuation objects, with complete released-state must-allow fixtures and malformed-state must-refuse fixtures. Do not tighten supported historical reads accidentally."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 3
tags[2]: follow-up,validation
created_at: "2026-10-30T14:39:41.610Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-30T14:39:48.587Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: Malformed persisted merge state refuses before new objects or namespace mutations; every previously supported serialized merge state still reads and continues or aborts correctly; a revert-proof regression covers each new refusal.
